  "body": "## Problem\n\nFour posts drop a bottom dwell on G73 (chip-break peck) and give no warning. The program runs with no dwell. The operator does not know.\n\nEach post has this line in `onCycle()`:\n\n```js\nif (ms > 0 && g !== \"G73\" && g !== \"G84\") words.push(\"P\" + ms);\n```\n\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:1076`\n- `assets/posts/haas.cps:913`\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps:902`\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps:1237`\n\nThe same line drops a G84 dwell without a warning too.\n\nThe Sinumerik post has the same pattern. #2354 tracks it, so it is not in this issue.\n\n## Expected\n\nEach post writes the dwell word that its control documents for G73, or it refuses the dwell by name with `msg()`. A dwell is never dropped silently (Prime Directive).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Check the published programming manual of each control for a P word on G73 and G84. Use behaviour only.\n- Found during #2349 / PR #2353. The `grblhal.cps` and `tormach.cps` posts were not checked (another worker has them, #2348).\n",
